--- Qwen3 prefill sweep: Hq=16 Hkv=8 (GQA group=2) D=128 causal ---
  Covers BOTH Qwen3-0.6B AND Qwen3-1.7B: their attention shapes are identical
  (16 Q heads / 8 KV heads / head_dim 128 / 28 layers). Only hidden_size differs
  (1024 vs 2048), which sizes the QKV projections and never reaches this kernel.
  GFLOP = causal-correct USEFUL flops = 4*Hq*D*#{(i,j): j<=i}, i.e. ~half of the
  non-causal 4*Hq*Sq*Sk*D. Timings are QEMU FUNCTIONAL EMULATION of one core --
  they measure work done, NOT hardware speed. Do not read them as ARM perf.
  [ref:N rows spread 0..Sq-1]: the fp32 ref checks N rows SPREAD over the whole
  sequence, incl. row Sq-1 -- which attends all Sk keys and so walks every key
  block and every online-softmax rescale. (A prefix of N rows would be causal-
  masked down to an NxN corner of the FIRST key block: same cost, no coverage.)
